{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F6h1RUiv4ZVcLe86fXgDQZ","type":"tool_result","content":"  loopless := ⟨fun _ h => h.1 rfl⟩\n\n/-- Delete every edge at `v`, leaving it isolated: vertex deletion on a fixed\nvertex type (the code's step `(v, -1)`). -/\ndef isolate (G : SimpleGraph V) (v : V) : SimpleGraph V where\n  Adj x y := G.Adj x y ∧ x ≠ v ∧ y ≠ v\n  symm := ⟨fun _ _ ⟨h, hx, hy⟩ => ⟨h.symm, hy, hx⟩⟩\n  loopless := ⟨fun x h => G.loopless.irrefl x h.1⟩\n\ntheorem isolate_le (G : SimpleGraph V) (v : V) : isolate G v ≤ G := fun _ _ h => h.1\n\n===WEIGHTS\n/-\nCopyright (c) 2026 Alexandre Linhares. All rights reserved.\nReleased under the MIT license as described in the file LICENSE.\n\n# The Edwards–McDermid weights `g = g_{1/6}` and `g'`\n\nEdwards & McDermid, *A general reduction theorem with applications to pathwidth and the\ncomplexity of MAX 2-CSP*, Algorithmica 72 (2015), Section 3.1 (p. 6–7) and Appendix\n(Lemmas 8.1, 8.3, 8.4, 8.5). This is item 03 of loop0012 (`reports/edwards_mcdermid_plan.md`\n§0.5; `reports/edwards_mcdermid.md` §3): the weight function the degree-sequence bound on\npathwidth is built from, with every property the reduction theorem (items 05–08) uses.\n\n* `g 0 = g 1 = g 2 = 0`, `g 3 = 1/6`, and `n g n = (n − 2) g (n − 1) + g (n − 2) + 1` for\n  `n ≥ 4` (`g_recurrence`); the table `1/6, 1/3, 13/30, 23/45, 359/630, 1553/2520,\n  14827/22680` at `n = 3..9` (`g_four` … `g_nine`, the paper's table p. 7 to `d = 8`).\n* `g' n = g n − g (n − 1)` (natural subtraction, so `g' 0 = 0`); `g' d = 0` for `d ≤ 2`.\n* Lemma 8.3 (`g_monotone`): `g` is non-decreasing, by the coupled invariant\n  `0 ≤ g n ≤ g (n + 1) ≤ (1 + g n) / 2`, `g n < 1` (`g_aux`); hence `g_nonneg`, `g_lt_one`.\n* Lemma 8.4 (`g'_antitone_of_three_le`): `g'` is non-increasing from 3, by the recurrence\n  `n g' n = (n − 3) g' (n − 1) + g' (n − 2)` for `n ≥ 5` (`g'_recurrence`) and the sandwich\n  `g' n / 3 ≤ g' (n + 1) ≤ g' n` (`g'_aux`); hence `g'_le_sixth`.\n* Property 6 (`one_sub_g_eq`): `1 − g n = (n − 1) g' n + g' (n − 1)` for `n ≥ 4`.\n* `g'_nonneg`, `g'_le_g`; Lemma 8.1 (`g_closed_form`): `g n = (7/2) A n / n! + (3/2) (−1)^n / n! − 5/2`\n  for `n ≥ 2`, `A` the alternating factorial; Lemma 8.5 (`g_div_lt_g_div`): `g n / n` is\n  strictly decreasing from `n = 5`.\n\nOnly `α = 1/6` is formalised (plan §0.5). Every statement was checked in exact rationals to\n`n = 200` before it was stated (`reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/03_weights/check.py`).\n-/\nimport Mathlib.Tactic\n\nnamespace MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound\n\n/-- The Edwards–McDermid weight `g_{1/6}`: `g 0 = g 1 = g 2 = 0`, `g 3 = 1/6`, and\n`n g n = (n − 2) g (n − 1) + g (n − 2) + 1` for `n ≥ 4` (p. 6). -/\ndef g : ℕ → ℚ\n  | 0 => 0\n  | 1 => 0\n  | 2 => 0\n  | 3 => 1 / 6\n  | n + 4 => (((n : ℚ) + 2) * g (n + 3) + g (n + 2) + 1) / ((n : ℚ) + 4)\n\n/-- `g' n = g n − g (n − 1)`, the marginal weight of one more edge at a vertex (p. 7). -/\ndef g' (n : ℕ) : ℚ := g n - g (n - 1)\n\n@[simp] theorem g_zero : g 0 = 0 := rfl\n@[simp] theorem g_one : g 1 = 0 := rfl\n@[simp] theorem g_two : g 2 = 0 := rfl\n@[simp] theorem g_three : g 3 = 1 / 6 := rfl\n\n/-- The defining recurrence in shifted form. -/\ntheorem g_add_four (n : ℕ) :\n    g (n + 4) = (((n : ℚ) + 2) * g (n + 3) + g (n + 2) + 1) / ((n : ℚ) + 4) := by\n  rw [g]\n\n/-- The defining recurrence, multiplied out. -/\ntheorem g_add_four_mul (n : ℕ) :\n    ((n : ℚ) + 4) * g (n + 4) = ((n : ℚ) + 2) * g (n + 3) + g (n + 2) + 1 := by\n  rw [g_add_four, mul_div_cancel₀]\n  positivity\n===NAMES\n36:def g : ℕ → ℚ\n44:def g' (n : ℕ) : ℚ := g n - g (n - 1)\n52:theorem g_add_four (n : ℕ) :\n57:theorem g_add_four_mul (n : ℕ) :\n63:theorem g_recurrence {n : ℕ} (hn : 4 ≤ n) :\n73:theorem g_four : g 4 = 1 / 3 := by norm_num [g_add_four]\n74:theorem g_five : g 5 = 13 / 30 := by norm_num [g_add_four]\n75:theorem g_six : g 6 = 23 / 45 := by norm_num [g_add_four]\n76:theorem g_seven : g 7 = 359 / 630 := by norm_num [g_add_four]\n77:theorem g_eight : g 8 = 1553 / 2520 := by norm_num [g_add_four]\n78:theorem g_nine : g 9 = 14827 / 22680 := by norm_num [g_add_four]\n81:theorem g_table :\n88:theorem g_aux (n : ℕ) :\n132:theorem g_nonneg (n : ℕ) : 0 ≤ g n := (g_aux n).1\n135:theorem g_lt_one (n : ℕ) : g n < 1 := (g_aux n).2.2.2\n137:theorem g_le_succ (n : ℕ) : g n ≤ g (n + 1) := (g_aux n).2.1\n140:theorem g_monotone : Monotone g := monotone_nat_of_le_succ g_le_succ\n142:theorem g'_succ (n : ℕ) : g' (n + 1) = g (n + 1) - g n := by simp [g']\n147:theorem g'_three : g' 3 = 1 / 6 := by simp [g']\n148:theorem g'_four : g' 4 = 1 / 6 := by rw [g'_succ, g_four, g_three]; norm_num\n149:theorem g'_five : g' 5 = 1 / 10 := by rw [g'_succ, g_five, g_four]; norm_num\n150:theorem g'_six : g' 6 = 7 / 90 := by rw [g'_succ, g_six, g_five]; norm_num\n151:theorem g'_seven : g' 7 = 37 / 630 := by rw [g'_succ, g_seven, g_six]; norm_num\n152:theorem g'_eight : g' 8 = 13 / 280 := by rw [g'_succ, g_eight, g_seven]; norm_num\n156:theorem g'_eq_zero_of_le_two {n : ℕ} (hn : n ≤ 2) : g' n = 0 := by\n160:theorem g'_nonneg (n : ℕ) : 0 ≤ g' n := by\n165:theorem g'_le_g (n : ℕ) : g' n ≤ g n := by\n170:theorem g'_add_five_mul (m : ℕ) :\n186:theorem g'_recurrence {n : ℕ} (hn : 5 ≤ n) :\n197:theorem g'_aux {n : ℕ} (hn : 3 ≤ n) : g' (n + 1) ≤ g' n ∧ g' n / 3 ≤ g' (n + 1) := by\n229:theorem g'_succ_le {n : ℕ} (hn : 3 ≤ n) : g' (n + 1) ≤ g' n := (g'_aux hn).1\n232:theorem g'_antitone_of_three_le {m n : ℕ} (hm : 3 ≤ m) (hmn : m ≤ n) : g' n ≤ g' m := by\n238:theorem g'_le_sixth (n : ℕ) : g' n ≤ 1 / 6 := by\n245:theorem one_sub_g_eq {n : ℕ} (hn : 4 ≤ n) :\n261:def altFactorial : ℕ → ℚ\n266:theorem altFactorial_succ (n : ℕ) :\n270:theorem g_closed_form {n : ℕ} (hn : 2 ≤ n) :\n305:theorem half_le_g {n : ℕ} (hn : 6 ≤ n) : 1 / 2 ≤ g n :=\n310:theorem g_div_lt_g_div {n : ℕ} (hn : 5 ≤ n) : g (n + 1) / ((n : ℚ) + 1) < g n / n := by","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7168600d-4bdf-441b-93a8-645b02e98376","u