{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0143322Rct7tES4Ww7toWPUa","type":"tool_result","content":"===CUT_HEADER\n/-\nCopyright (c) 2026 Alexandre Linhares. All rights reserved.\nReleased under the MIT license as described in the file LICENSE.\n\n# The cut lemma and its iterated form\n\nItem 04 of loop0012 (`reports/edwards_mcdermid_plan.md` §0.4 (3), §0.5;\n`reports/edwards_mcdermid.md` §2.1 (2) and §4): the one-cut transfer — a vertex\npartition with its two boundaries bounds the pathwidth of the whole by the\npathwidths of the two sides — and its recursive iteration. Neither depends on\nthe two named hypotheses of the Edwards–McDermid formalisation\n(`CubicPathwidthBound`, `ReductionPathwidthBound`, item 09); both are tools for\nevery graph.\n\n* `boundaryTo G A B` — the vertices of `A` with a neighbour in `B`;\n  `boundary G A` — the vertices of `A` with a neighbour outside `A`\n  (`boundary_eq_boundaryTo_compl`).\n* `pathwidth_induce_mono` — `T ⊆ U → pathwidth G[T] ≤ pathwidth G[U]`.\n* `pathwidth_induce_le_induce_add_card_sdiff` — `pathwidth G[U] ≤ pathwidth G[T] + |U ∖ T|` for\n  any two vertex sets, the relative form of `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl`\n  (`TreeBound.lean`); the brute-force check had it for `T ⊆ U` and the proof needed no\n  inclusion, so the check was extended to every pair.\n* `pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_boundaryTo` — for disjoint `S₁`, `S₂`,\n  `pathwidth G[S₁ ∪ S₂] ≤ max (pathwidth G[S₁]) (pathwidth G[S₂]) + |∂(S₁ → S₂)|`:\n  delete the boundary (the lemma above), the rest is a disjoint union with no edge\n  between the sides (`pathwidth_induce_union_le_max`), and `G[S₁ ∖ ∂] ≤ G[S₁]`.\n* **C1s** `pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_min` (relative) and\n  `pathwidth_le_max_add_min_boundary` (global): the separator form\n  `pathwidth G ≤ max (pathwidth G[S]) (pathwidth G[Sᶜ]) + min |∂S| |∂Sᶜ|`.\n* **C1** `pathwidth_le_cut`: the item's three-term form\n  `pathwidth G ≤ max (max (pathwidth G[S] + |∂S|) (pathwidth G[Sᶜ] + |∂Sᶜ|)) (|∂S| + |∂Sᶜ| − 1)`,\n  a corollary of C1s (`max a b + min c d ≤ max (a + c) (b + d)`); stated as the\n  item asks, with the `− 1` in `ℕ`.\n* **C2s** `BisectionTree G S bs k` — a recursive bisection of `S` given level by level:\n  `bs = []` means `pathwidth G[S] ≤ k`; `bs = b :: bs'` means `S` splits into two\n  disjoint parts whose smaller boundary (`min`) has at most `b` vertices, each part\n  carrying a `BisectionTree` for `bs'`. `pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTree`:\n  `BisectionTree G univ bs k → pathwidth G ≤ k + bs.sum`; by induction on `bs` through\n  the relative C1s, so it never needs a nested `induce`.\n* **C2** `BisectionTreeMax` is the same with the larger boundary (`max`) budgeted, as the\n  item's text has it; it implies `BisectionTree` (`bisectionTree_of_bisectionTreeMax`),\n  and `pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax_two_mul` is the item's `pathwidth G ≤ k + 2 bs.sum`\n  (the factor 2 is slack: `pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax` has `k + bs.sum`).\n\n**What these lemmas do not give.** Fomin & Høie (2006) reach `pw ≤ (1/6 + ε) n` for\ncubic graphs with **one** level — a Monien–Preis bisection with at most `(1/6 + ε/2) n`\ncut edges, their Lemma 4 on each side (a path decomposition of a graph of maximum degree\n3 of width at most `max{|X|, n/3 + 1} + (2/3) log₃ n + 1` whose *last* bag is a\nprescribed set `X`), and a sweep across the boundary that holds the middle bags at\n`|∂V₁| + 1` — not by iterating C2: iterating C2s with Monien–Preis cuts of `(1/6 + ε)`\nof each piece sums to `n/3`. Lemma 4 and the sweep are stated in\n`reports/edwards_mcdermid.md` §4 and are not proved here.\n\nEvery statement was checked by brute force before it was stated\n(`reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/04_cut/check.py`): the relative forms on every\nordered pair of disjoint vertex sets of every graph to 7 vertices, the global forms on\nevery partition, the bisection forms on 2,000 random graphs at 10–12 vertices.\n-/\nimport MOSPFormalization.TreeBound\nimport MOSPFormalization.Minor\n\nset_option linter.unusedSectionVars false\n\nnamespace MOSPFormalization\n\nvariable {V : Type*} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\nvariable (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n\n/-! ### Boundaries -/\n\n===COMPONENTS_IN_REPO\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Mycielski.lean:344:/-! ### Lower bound: restricting a decomposition to a connected set -/\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Sandwich.lean:645:def PathDecomposition.restrict (P : PathDecomposition G) (A : Finset V) :\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Sandwich.lean:713:restricting `P` to `A` gives a decomposition of `G[A]`, whose largest bag has at least\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Sandwich.lean:718:  have hle : k ≤ (P.restrict A).width := hA.trans (pathwidth_le_width _ (P.restrict A))\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Sandwich.lean:721:    ⟨⟨0, Nat.zero_lt_succ _⟩⟩) (fun i : Fin ((P.restrict A).length + 1) => ((P.restrict A).bag i).card)\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Sandwich.lean:723:  have hpos : 1 ≤ ((P.restrict A).bag i).card := by\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Sandwich.lean:726:    have h1 : 1 ≤ ((P.restrict A).bag j).card :=\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Sandwich.lean:729:    exact h1.trans (Finset.le_sup' (fun i : Fin ((P.restrict A).length + 1) =>\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Sandwich.lean:730:      ((P.restrict A).bag i).card) (Finset.mem_univ j))\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Sandwich.lean:732:    have : ((P.restrict A).bag i).card = ((P.bag i).filter (fun x => x ∈ A)).card :=\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:57:* `restrictOff G S` (the edges of `G` with both ends off `S`), `pairsOff S`,\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:58:  `pairsMeeting S`; `isBalancedBip_restrictOff` (`E_bip(S)` depends on `G` only\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:60:  for `H` with no edge meeting `S`, the graphs `G` with `restrictOff G S = H` have\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:369:  ∃ p : G.Walk u v, ∀ w ∈ p.support, w ∉ S\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:380:    {u v : V} (p : G.Walk u v) (hp : ∀ w ∈ p.support, w ∉ S) (hu : u ∈ A) : v ∈ A := by\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:384:    have hq : ∀ w ∈ q.support, w ∉ S := fun w hw =>\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:536:def restrictOff (S : Finset V) : SimpleGraph V where\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:547:theorem restrictOff_adj {S : Finset V} {u v : V} :\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:548:    (restrictOff G S).Adj u v ↔ G.Adj u v ∧ u ∉ S ∧ v ∉ S := Iff.rfl\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:550:theorem restrictOff_restrictOff (S : Finset V) :\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:551:    restrictOff (restrictOff G S) S = restrictOff G S := by\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:553:  simp only [restrictOff_adj]\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:598:theorem edges_restrictOff (S : Finset V) :\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:599:    edges (restrictOff G S) = (edges G).filter (AvoidsSet S) := by\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:604:      restrictOff_adj, avoidsSet_mk]\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:607:theorem edges_subset_pairsOff_of_restrictOff_eq {S : Finset V} {H : SimpleGraph V}\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:608:    (hH : restrictOff H S = H) : edges H ⊆ pairsOff S := by\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:610:  rw [← hH, edges_restrictOff] at he\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:615:theorem isBalancedBip_restrictOff (S : Finset V) (k : ℕ) :\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:616:    IsBalancedBip (restrictOff G S) S k ↔ IsBalancedBip G S k := by\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:618:      (IsEmptyPair (restrictOff G S) A R ↔ IsEmptyPair G A R) := by\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:641:on `V` with `restrictOff G S = H` are the unions of `H` with a subset of the pairs meeting\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:645:theorem sum_gnpWeight_fiber (S : Finset V) {H : SimpleGraph V} (hH : restrictOff H S = H)\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:647:    ∑ G ∈ (univ : Finset (SimpleGraph V)).filter (fun G => restrictOff G S = H), gnpWeight p G =\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:649:  have hEH : edges H ⊆ pairsOff S := edges_subset_pairsOff_of_restrictOff_eq hH\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:659:      ∑ G ∈ (univ : Finset (SimpleGraph V)).filter (fun G => restrictOff G S = H),\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:669:      rw [restrictOff_adj, SimpleGraph.fromEdgeSet_adj, mem_coe, mem_union]\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:695:      have hG' : restrictOff G S = H := (mem_filter.1 hG).2\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:697:        rw [← hG', edges_restrictOff]\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:730:  classical exact univ.filter (fun H => restrictOff H S = H)\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:733:    H ∈ offGraphs S ↔ restrictOff H S = H := by\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:744:      restrictOff G S ∈ (offGraphs S).filter (fun H => IsBalancedBip H S k) := by\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:746:    rw [mem_filter, mem_offGraphs, restrictOff_restrictOff, isBalancedBip_restrictOff]\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:760:    rw [← isBalancedBip_restrictOff, h]\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:903:theorem restrictOff_relabel {e : V ≃ V} {S₀ S : Finset V} (hS : ∀ x, e x ∈ S ↔ x ∈ S₀)\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:904:    (G : SimpleGraph V) : restrictOff (relabel e G) S = relabel e (restrictOff G S₀) := by\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:906:  rw [restrictOff_adj, relabel_adj, relabel_adj, restrictOff_adj]\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:957:    rw [restrictOff_relabel hS, hH.1]\nlean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean:961:    rw [restrictOff_relabel hS', hH.1]\nlean/MOSPFormalization/TreeBound.lean:28:  Proved by induction on `|S|`, splitting off the reachability class `reachSet G S v`.","is_error":fa